From: hurrhnn <hurrhnn@icmp.kr>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 00:30:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] net: pcs: airoha: debounce the rxlock workaround

The rxlock workaround fires a destructive CDR reset off a single
instantaneous PCS status read, although the SigDet scan that precedes
the reset takes a while and the RX may have recovered on its own in the
meantime.

Re-read the PCS status after the SigDet scan and skip the CDR reset if
the RX link is up again.

Signed-off-by: hurrhnn <hurrhnn@icmp.kr>
---
--- a/drivers/net/pcs/airoha/pcs-an7581.c
+++ b/drivers/net/pcs/airoha/pcs-an7581.c
@@ -2081,6 +2081,10 @@
 	if (!an7581_pcs_have_rx_signal(priv, index))
 		return 0;

+	regmap_read(maps->usxgmii_pcs, AIROHA_PCS_USXGMII_PCS_STUS_1, &val);
+	if (val & AIROHA_PCS_USXGMII_PCS_RX_LINK_STATUS_UP)
+		return 0;
+
 	/* If PCS is down but RX SigDet module detected signal,
 	 * trigger CDR reset.
 	 */
